<title>FRANCE: GEC Alsthom confirms cruise ships deal.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom confirms cruise ships deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-08-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipyard Chantiers de l'Atlantique, a subsidiary of GEC Alsthom NV, has received a firm order for two 370-cabin cruise ships from U.S. company Renaissance Cruise.</p>
<p>In a statement GEC Alsthom said the contract was confirming a letter of intent signed earlier this year.</p>
<p>The two ships are due to be delivered in June 1998 and February 1999.</p>
<p>According to trade unions the contract is worth some $500 million or 2.5 billion francs and includes an option on a third ship.</p>
<p>GEC Alsthom is a joint venture between Britain's General Electric Co Pl. and France's Alcatel Alsthom.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
